WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.920
In the 2021 live-action "Mortal Kombat" movie
there are two main factions fighting against

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.920
one another.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.780
On one side are a rag-tag group of warriors
brought together by Lord Raiden to train in

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.490
order to protect Earthrealm from being overtaken
by the forces of Outworld.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.080
On the other side is a sinister collection
of fighters assembled by the sorcerer Shang

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.490
Tsung whose goal is to eliminate Earthrealm's
defenders.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.890
Among Shang Tsung's henchpeople is the winged
hunter Nitara.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.300
All in all, Nitara has a very small role in
this version of the "Mortal Kombat" story.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.310
While fans of the character are no doubt thrilled
to see her included, she doesn't serve much

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.900
purpose in the action of the film other than
to be introduced to Kung Lao's hat buzzsaw.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.590
She may not be the most consequential character
in the world of the game series, but she does

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.230
have much more backstory than the movie chose
to include.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.620
From her mysterious origins to her distinct
motivations, Nitara is a unique character

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.510
in the annals of "Mortal Kombat" history.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:52.870
Here's what only those who have a deep knowledge
of "Mortal Kombat" lore know about Nitara.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:57.110
Nitara's bat-like wings and ability to fly
sets her apart from the rest of the characters

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.050
introduced in the "Mortal Kombat" film.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.070
The movie doesn't dive deep into this, but
Nitara is a member of a vampire species from

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.350
the vampire realm.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.650
She has the distinction of being one of the
only representatives of her species in the

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.080
"Mortal Kombat" canon.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.970
The character debuted in the 2002 game "Mortal
Kombat: Deadly Alliance," a revival of sorts

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:17.140
for the franchise that introduced new mechanics
and characters.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.820
Nitara and her vampiric kin are described
as traveling among the many realms looking

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.990
for other beings to feast on.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:27.060
Similar to other vampiric legends, the vampires
of "Mortal Kombat" are unable to withstand

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.570
the rays of the sun of Earthrealm and are
only able to feed on humans at night.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.240
"Hey do you know if any of this stuff is organic?"

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.270
"Just asking, jeez."

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.119
At some point before the action of "Deadly
Alliance," Nitara's realm was subsumed into

00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:42.260
Outworld by its emperor Shao Kahn.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.790
Her motivation throughout the action of the
game is to secure a magical orb that will

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.830
enable her to free her realm from Outworld's
control.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:53.320
During Nitara's short stint in the 2021 "Mortal
Kombat" film, she mostly acts as one of Shang

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.100
Tsung's lackeys, similar to Kabal and Mileena.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.560
However, while working with the baddies isn't
out of character for her, in the world of

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.740
the video games, the only person Nitara has
allegiance to is herself and her people.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.340
While many of the characters in the "Mortal
Kombat" canon either fall on the side of good

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.329
or evil, Nitara is distinctly neutral.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:13.319
When she was introduced in "Deadly Alliance,"
her motivations were solely to destroy the

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:16.099
magical orb that is keeping her realm tethered
to Outworld.

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:20.560
She uses deception and manipulation to get
other characters to help her with this task.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.669
"Deadly Alliance" even reveals that she helped
facilitate the execution of Outworld Emperor

00:02:24.669 --> 00:02:29.010
Shao Khan, but only because it happened to
help advance her personal agenda.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.590
As the character gets little screen time during
the film, it's hard to say exactly what her

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:35.090
motivations for teaming up with Shang Tsung
are.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.779
But if she is anything like her video game
counterpart, she was likely much less loyal

00:02:38.779 --> 00:02:40.280
to him than it appears.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.709
Like many other fighting game franchises,
"Mortal Kombat" is known for having characters

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:47.090
come back for multiple repeat appearances
throughout the series.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.519
Despite the fact that she's one of the more
unique fighters, though, Nitara is also one

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:53.219
of the more underutilized characters in the
franchise.

00:02:53.219 --> 00:02:57.610
The only three games to feature her as a playable
character are "Mortal Kombat: Deadly Alliance,"

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:02.239
"Mortal Kombat: Armageddon," and the GameBoy
Advance entry "Mortal Kombat: Tournament Edition."

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:05.840
She has been referenced and made cameo appearances
in other games, though.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.889
"I stepped out with Nitara before you.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.209
You clearly have a type, Erron."

00:03:12.209 --> 00:03:16.170
Nitara's elusive nature in the game series
makes it even more of a thrill that she was

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.379
included in the "Mortal Kombat" film, even
if it was a brief appearance.

